  <data name="labelBCISignalCheckDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>BCI signal quality is an indicator of  how good the contact is between the electrodes on the cap and your scalp. 

ACAT uses two metrics - “railing” and “impedance” - to check signal quality for each connected electrode. The slider below gives an indication of the overall quality</value>
  </data>
